  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{4}$ by $3$, we repeat the fraction model $3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14128162/assets/52b2f58e97058deb1cbe8c01cd1ab430261c3a9f8f374a6cb650ebf0931553e9.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $3\\times 1=3$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n3\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$",
